# 3. PostgreSQL Configuration

## 3.1 Main configuration files

| File | Purpose |
|---|---|
| postgresql.conf | Main instance-level configuration. |
| postgresql.auto.conf | Stores ALTER SYSTEM changes; read after postgresql.conf, so it overrides it. |
| pg_hba.conf | Client authentication rules; not managed by ALTER SYSTEM. |
| pg_ident.conf | Maps external/OS usernames to PostgreSQL roles when used with pg_hba.conf map rules. |

## 3.2 Split configuration

```text
include_dir = 'conf.d'
include_file = 'memory.conf'
include = 'autovacuum.conf'
```

- `include_dir` can contain multiple files; files are read in filename order.
- `include_file` refers to one file.
- `ALTER SYSTEM` writes to `postgresql.auto.conf`.

```sql
ALTER SYSTEM RESET work_mem;
ALTER SYSTEM RESET ALL;

SELECT pg_reload_conf();

SELECT name, setting, sourcefile, sourceline
FROM pg_settings;
```

## 3.3 pg_settings vs pg_db_role_settings

| View | Use |
|---|---|
| pg_settings | Shows the effective runtime setting and metadata such as source file and context. |
| pg_db_role_settings | Shows settings applied specifically through ALTER DATABASE ... SET and ALTER ROLE ... SET. |

## 3.4 Configuration context — interview version

| Context | Meaning | Examples |
|---|---|---|
| internal | Fixed; cannot be changed at runtime. | block_size, server_version |
| postmaster | Requires full restart. | shared_buffers, max_connections, wal_level, port |
| sighup | Change config + reload. | many logging/checkpoint settings |
| backend / superuser-backend | Takes effect at backend/session start. | session-start parameters |
| superuser | Superuser can change it in a session. | parameter-dependent |
| user | User can SET it for their session. | work_mem, search_path, statement_timeout |

> ⭐ Before changing a parameter: `SELECT name, setting, context FROM pg_settings WHERE name = 'parameter_name';`

