# 13. Logical Replication

| Concept | Meaning |
|---|---|
| Publisher | Source side where publications are defined. |
| Publication | Defines which tables/operations are published. |
| Subscriber | Destination side that subscribes to publications. |
| Table sync worker | Used during initial table synchronization. |
| Apply worker | Applies logical changes on the subscriber. |
| Replication slot | Tracks logical decoding progress. |

- Logical replication replicates row-level changes rather than the whole physical database.
- Table structure is not automatically reproduced as a physical copy; the target schema must be prepared appropriately.
- Primary keys are important for identifying rows for `UPDATE` / `DELETE` in common configurations.
- `pglogical` is an extension that provides additional logical replication capabilities.

