# 15. pgBackRest

## 15.1 Core concepts

| Concept | Remember |
|---|---|
| Stanza | Identity/name for a PostgreSQL cluster configuration in pgBackRest. |
| Archive-push | Moves WAL into the pgBackRest repository. |
| Full | Complete backup. |
| Differential | Changes since the last full backup. |
| Incremental | Changes since the latest applicable backup. |
| Retention | Controls how many backups are retained. |
| Restore | Restores a physical backup to a target data directory. |
| PITR | Restore a backup and replay WAL to a target time. |

```text
[global]
repo1-path=/dba_instance/dbrepo
repo1-retention-full=2
process-max=2
start-fast=y

[main]
pg1-path=/var/lib/pgsql/17/data
pg1-port=5432

archive_command = 'pgbackrest --stanza=main archive-push %p'

pgbackrest --stanza=main stanza-create
pgbackrest --stanza=main backup --type=full
pgbackrest --stanza=main backup --type=diff
pgbackrest --stanza=main backup --type=incr

pgbackrest info --stanza=main
pgbackrest --stanza=main restore
pgbackrest --stanza=main --set=<backup-set> restore
pgbackrest --stanza=main --type=time --target="YYYY-MM-DD HH:MI:SS" restore
```

> ⭐ pgBackRest = production-oriented physical backup + WAL archive + restore + PITR platform.

## 15.2 Backup verification

A backup is not trustworthy until it has been restored and tested. Periodically restore to a test/DR environment and validate PostgreSQL startup, data availability, and required objects.

