# 17. PostgreSQL High Availability

## 17.1 Patroni

Patroni is an HA framework for PostgreSQL. It manages leader election and failover using a distributed configuration store (DCS) and coordinates PostgreSQL roles.

| Concept | Remember |
|---|---|
| Leader lock | Patroni continuously renews the leader key/lock before its TTL expires. |
| DCS | Distributed store used for cluster coordination; examples include etcd, Consul, and ZooKeeper. |
| Failover | Promotion of a suitable replica when the leader is lost. |
| Switchover | Planned role change. |
| patronictl list | Quick cluster health/role view. |
| HAProxy | Can route client traffic toward the appropriate PostgreSQL node. |

## 17.2 repmgr

`repmgr` provides PostgreSQL replication and cluster management features such as monitoring, switchover/failover, and standby registration. For interviews, understand the purpose and operational workflow of cluster automation rather than just the command names.

## 17.3 HAProxy + PgBouncer

```text
Application
    ↓
HAProxy / connection layer
    ↓
PgBouncer (optional)
    ↓
Current PostgreSQL primary
    ├── standby
    └── standby
```

The exact architecture depends on the HA tooling and environment.

