# 19. Partitioning

Partitioning splits one logical table into smaller physical partitions while the application can still query the parent table.

| Type | Use |
|---|---|
| RANGE | Date ranges or numeric ranges. |
| LIST | Specific values/categories. |
| HASH | Distribute rows based on a hash of the partition key. |

```sql
CREATE TABLE orders (
    order_id bigint,
    order_date date,
    customer_id bigint
) PARTITION BY RANGE (order_date);
```

## 19.1 Partition pruning

When a query contains conditions that let PostgreSQL identify which partitions could contain matching rows, PostgreSQL can avoid scanning irrelevant partitions.

> ⭐ RANGE → dates/ranges | LIST → categories | HASH → distribution | PRUNING → skip irrelevant partitions

