## 20.2 Slow query troubleshooting sequence

```text
1. pg_stat_activity
2. Check waits / blocking / transaction age
3. EXPLAIN (ANALYZE, BUFFERS)
4. Compare estimated vs actual rows
5. Check Seq Scan / Index Scan / Bitmap Scan
6. Check Nested Loop / Hash Join / Merge Join
7. Check statistics / ANALYZE
8. Check index usage and bloat
9. Check work_mem / temp spills
10. Check CPU / memory / disk I/O
11. Check recent data/config/schema changes
```

## 20.3 General database slowdown sequence

```text
CPU / Memory
   ↓
Disk space / IOPS / latency
   ↓
Connections
   ↓
Long-running / blocked sessions
   ↓
Locks
   ↓
Slow queries / execution plans
   ↓
VACUUM / autovacuum
   ↓
Table / index bloat
   ↓
WAL generation / checkpoints
   ↓
Replication lag
   ↓
Backup status
   ↓
Logs
```

