# Final Quick Cheat Sheet

## Architecture

> PostgreSQL flow: connection → authentication → parser → analyzer → rewrite → planner → executor → result

## Security

> `pg_hba.conf` decides whether you can connect. Privileges decide what you can do after connection.

## Performance basics

> `effective_cache_size` is a planner estimate, not memory allocation.

> `work_mem` is per operation; sorts and hashes can spill to temp files when insufficient.

## VACUUM / MVCC

> MVCC keeps multiple row versions. VACUUM removes dead tuples and prevents wraparound issues.

## Replication / HA

> Physical streaming replication moves WAL from primary to standby.

> `pg_rewind` re-syncs an old primary after failover.

## Backup / recovery

> PITR = base backup + archived WAL + recovery target + replay.

> `pg_dump` is logical; `pg_basebackup` and `pgBackRest` are physical.

## Monitoring

> Start with `pg_stat_activity`, then `EXPLAIN (ANALYZE, BUFFERS)`, then memory / I/O / lock checks.

